":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/tiktok-aigc-video.json","type":"json","lines":23,"executable":false,"size_bytes":572,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/tiktok-app-draft.json","type":"json","lines":20,"executable":false,"size_bytes":501,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/tiktok-carousel.json","type":"json","lines":18,"executable":false,"size_bytes":647,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/tiktok-video.json","type":"json","lines":23,"executable":false,"size_bytes":564,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/x-first-comment.json","type":"json","lines":12,"executable":false,"size_bytes":446,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/x-retweet.json","type":"json","lines":13,"executable":false,"size_bytes":262,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/youtube-short.json","type":"json","lines":24,"executable":false,"size_bytes":879,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/youtube-video-captions.json","type":"json","lines":24,"executable":false,"size_bytes":676,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/youtube-video-thumbnail.json","type":"json","lines":24,"executable":false,"size_bytes":831,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/api-reference.md","type":"markdown","lines":508,"executable":false,"size_bytes":31730,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/media-specs.md","type":"markdown","lines":105,"executable":false,"size_bytes":4367,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/platform-controls.md","type":"markdown","lines":220,"executable":false,"size_bytes":15761,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/upload-flow.md","type":"markdown","lines":196,"executable":false,"size_bytes":6023,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-a38cde8ed3a84d9ea0e8b1776cdf7675","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":155,"end_line":null},"finding":"DELETE /social-posts/:id`.","explanation":"Tool parameters are crafted to achieve unintended or unsafe behavior. Parameter abuse can bypass intended safety checks (e.g. shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"  -d '{ \"ids\": [\"POST_ID_1\", \"POST_ID_2\"] }'\n```\n\nReturns `200` (not 201) with `{ \"deletedIds\": [...], \"notFoundIds\": [...] }`. `notFoundIds` holds ids that don't exist or belong to another workspace; a repeated id is reported once, and repeating the same call is harmless. `ids` takes 1-100 UUIDs: `[]` returns `400` \"At least one id is required\", more than 100 returns `400` \"ids cannot exceed 100 entries\", a non-UUID returns `400` \"Each id must be a valid UUID\". One call counts as one request against this endpoint's own limit, separate from `DELETE /social-posts/:id`.\n\n**Delete everything that matches a filter** (for example every scheduled post on one account, after the user confirmed): don't advance `page` while deleting, because later posts shift onto pages you have already read and get skipped. Instead repeat: read `GET /social-posts?socialMediaIds=ACCOUNT_ID&statuses=SCHEDULED&page=0&limit=50`, send the returned ids to `POST /social-posts/bulk-delete`, and stop when `data` comes back empty. Stop on any error too; after a `429`, wait `Retry-After` seconds, then run the loop again.\n","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"8f2fd4cde863a377e1115042f4bc541b5228ac863d1f024e2c59545480ce4a31","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":155,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-e567760c0d564b56962b294a607e1c08","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":640,"end_line":null},"finding":"DELETE /social-posts/:id`","explanation":"Tool parameters are crafted to achieve unintended or unsafe behavior. Parameter abuse can bypass intended safety checks (e.g. shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"|---|---|\n| `POST /social-posts` (up to 15 posts per call) | 180/minute, 420/day |\n| `GET /social-posts` | 720/hour, 7,200/day |\n| `DELETE /social-posts/:id` | 200/hour |\n| `POST /social-posts/bulk-delete` (up to 100 ids per call) | 200/hour |\n| `GET /social-posts/analytics` | 1,260/hour, 12,600/day |\n| `POST /file/get-signed-upload-urls` | 180/minute, 420/day |","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"25cf31923a183c0191940d672f867b7b45d120c1e05c9dcf42fdeae6edb98dc3","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":640,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-e567760c0d564b56962b294a607e1c08","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":656,"end_line":null},"finding":"DELETE /social-posts/:id`","explanation":"Tool parameters are crafted to achieve unintended or unsafe behavior. Parameter abuse can bypass intended safety checks (e.g. shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"|---|---|\n| `POST /social-posts` (up to 15 posts per call) | 180/minute, 420/day |\n| `GET /social-posts` | 720/hour, 7,200/day |\n| `DELETE /social-posts/:id` | 200/hour |\n| `POST /social-posts/bulk-delete` (up to 100 ids per call) | 200/hour |\n| `GET /social-posts/analytics` | 1,260/hour, 12,600/day |\n| `POST /file/get-signed-upload-urls` | 180/minute, 420/day |","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"25cf31923a183c0191940d672f867b7b45d120c1e05c9dcf42fdeae6edb98dc3","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":656,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-e567760c0d564b56962b294a607e1c08","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":725,"end_line":null},"finding":"DELETE /social-posts/:id`","explanation":"Tool parameters are crafted to achieve unintended or unsafe behavior. Parameter abuse can bypass intended safety checks (e.g. shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"|---|---|\n| `POST /social-posts` (up to 15 posts per call) | 180/minute, 420/day |\n| `GET /social-posts` | 720/hour, 7,200/day |\n| `DELETE /social-posts/:id` | 200/hour |\n| `POST /social-posts/bulk-delete` (up to 100 ids per call) | 200/hour |\n| `GET /social-posts/analytics` | 1,260/hour, 12,600/day |\n| `POST /file/get-signed-upload-urls` | 180/minute, 420/day |","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"25cf31923a183c0191940d672f867b7b45d120c1e05c9dcf42fdeae6edb98dc3","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":725,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-36f0786c118e44a4abd1341cdf85a478","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":840,"end_line":null},"finding":"DELETE /social-posts/:id","explanation":"Tool parameters are crafted to achieve unintended or unsafe behavior. Parameter abuse can bypass intended safety checks (e.g. shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"GET /social-posts?ids=POST_ID_1,POST_ID_2\n\n# Delete posts (PostFast only: a published post stays live on the platform)\nDELETE /social-posts/:id                            -> { deleted: true | false }\nPOST   /social-posts/bulk-delete  { ids: [1-100] }  -> { deletedIds, notFoundIds }\n\n# Upload media (3 steps)","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"ee970d8bab906c21e4a95c82289dafbabc96104b4a63b07a0f7bfb9db552a070","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":840,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-93da3ee67ea34d53975b6e03cda90f88","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"references/api-reference.md","start_line":381,"end_line":null},"finding":"DELETE /social-posts/:id","explanation":"The skill exposes a destructive delete capability for any post status and the documentation does not pair it with strong guardrails such as mandatory confirmation, pre-deletion lookup, or scope validation. In an agent setting, this increases the chance that ambiguous, injected, or mistaken inputs could trigger unauthorized deletion of user-managed content within the workspace.","remediation":"Require explicit user confirmation before every delete call, and fetch/display the target post details for verification first. Enforce strict parameter validation against user intent, log destructive actions, and add policy text that deletion must never be inferred from vague requests.","code_snippet":"| YouTube post with a caption key but no `youtubeLanguage` | `youtubeCaptionKey.languageRequired` |\n| Unknown `youtubeLanguage` code on a YouTube post | `youtubeLanguage.invalid` |\n\n### DELETE /social-posts/:id\n\nDelete one post, in any status. Rate limit: 200/hour.\n","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"ee970d8bab906c21e4a95c82289dafbabc96104b4a63b07a0f7bfb9db552a070","occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-reference.md","start_line":381,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-ea847f793ccb4a1988f4dc7d792bc563","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/api-reference.md","start_line":395,"end_line":null},"finding":"DELETE /social-posts/:id`);","explanation":"Bulk deletion of up to 100 posts per call materially increases the blast radius of parameter abuse in an agent workflow. If an attacker can influence filters, IDs, or prompt interpretation, the agent could remove large sets of scheduled or draft posts from the workspace without adequate user awareness, causing significant operational disruption.","remediation":"Add mandatory confirmation with a summary of the exact IDs/count to be deleted before execution. Require a dry-run/list step first, cap automated deletions conservatively, and block bulk-delete unless the user explicitly requests deletion of the enumerated results.","code_snippet":"\n### POST /social-posts/bulk-delete\n\nDelete up to 100 posts in one request. Rate limit: 200/hour (its own budget, separate from `DELETE /social-posts/:id`); one call counts as one request.\n\n**Request:**\n```json","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"caacacea4d05b2d7ab5335ed47011aff313f621bcba9259c931038b37afddee8","occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-reference.md","start_line":395,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-7f6862b4e43f49ea950f06aa98f23063","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/api-reference.md","start_line":409,"end_line":null},"finding":"DELETE /social-posts/:id`:","explanation":"The guidance to repeatedly read page 0 and continue bulk-deleting until empty is effectively a recipe for mass deletion. In an autonomous or semi-autonomous agent context, this creates a dangerous amplification pattern where a single mistaken filter or manipulated instruction can erase all matching posts in the workspace.","remediation":"Remove or heavily qualify the 'delete everything matching a filter' automation guidance for agent use. Replace it with a staged workflow: preview results, require explicit confirmation of total scope, delete in small batches, and re-confirm before continuing across multiple iterations.","code_snippet":"\n- `ids` is required: 1-100 post UUIDs, each a UUID v4. `[]` returns `400` \"At least one id is required\", more than 100 returns `400` \"ids cannot exceed 100 entries\", a non-UUID returns `400` \"Each id must be a valid UUID\".\n- `notFoundIds` holds the ids that don't exist or belong to another workspace (both get the same answer). A repeated id is reported once, and repeating a call with the same ids is harmless (they all come back in `notFoundIds`).\n- Deletes the same way as `DELETE /social-posts/:id`: any status, PostFast only, published posts stay live on the platform.\n- **Delete everything that matches a filter:** re-read `GET /social-posts` at `page=0` with the same filter and bulk-delete what it returns until it comes back empty. Stop on any error, including a `429`; wait `Retry-After` seconds and continue.\n\n### GET /social-posts/analytics","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"ec2ebb85e4e667257edc35b8e19cda441e9ae3e1b7d1f87cd10f504556cd7136","occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-reference.md","start_line":409,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-a7c693c0c5f5439d932ca2450ebcd288","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":32,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -s -H \"pf-api-key: $POSTFAST_API_KEY\" https://api.postfa.st/social-media/my-social-accounts\n```\n\nReturns array of `{ id, platform, platformUsername, displayName, connectionStatus, disabledReason,","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"### 1. List connected accounts\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -H \"pf-api-key: $POSTFAST_API_KEY\" https://api.postfa.st/social-media/my-social-accounts\n```\n\nReturns array of `{ id, platform, platformUsername, displayName, connectionStatus, disabledReason, inboxCapable, followerCount?, followerCountUpdatedAt? }`. Save the `id` (the `socialMediaId` required for every post).","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"8a14c246e27ce91c7674d1c27bc5298287ce17af65d4c61a2a71c495de13e5f6","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":32,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-d993a240224c4d9f9f08b496ef270440","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":168,"end_line":null},"finding":"https://api.postfa.st/","explanation":"The connect-link endpoint creates a bearer-style onboarding URL that lets whoever opens it attach social accounts to the workspace. Because the skill explicitly notes that the URL should be treated like a credential, accidental disclosure by an agent or unsafe sharing behavior could grant unauthorized account-linking capability to third parties.","remediation":"Treat generated connect URLs as secrets: never echo them into public channels, logs, or shared transcripts; only deliver them to the intended recipient after explicit confirmation. Add guardrails requiring confirmation of destination, minimize retention, and redact or suppress the tokenized URL from routine agent outputs/logging where possible.","code_snippet":"Let clients connect their social accounts to your workspace without creating a PostFast account:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://api.postfa.st/social-media/connect-link \\\n  -H \"pf-api-key: $POSTFAST_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"aa8d70e9b18461bfce78a3e3a63df6d072055fbb1c3be7fb27250147faa6f9fa","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":168,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-010b70c8fcae4cb9af3cce7cd3aad0ee","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":219,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -X POST https://api.postfa.st/social-posts \\\n  -H \"pf-api-key: $POSTFAST_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"posts\": [{ \"content\": \"Draft idea...\", \"mediaItems\": [], \"","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"**PostFast draft (recommended for \"save now, schedule later\"):**\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://api.postfa.st/social-posts \\\n  -H \"pf-api-key: $POSTFAST_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"32984cd68e642cd17aa2fc031ca10548c5e117992b2de76e92901f67a9f6859f","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":219,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-2df2798027e24d3fa698917e8e3f3130","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"examples/EXAMPLES.md","start_line":40,"end_line":44},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes an example for `POST /social-posts/bulk-delete` and explains its usage, but it does not warn that the operation can remove up to 100 posts and may be irreversible or impactful to user data. For markdown files, destructive behaviors should be disclosed so users understand the risk before using the example.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the `bulk-delete.json` entry or in the Usage section stating that bulk delete permanently removes selected posts, should be used carefully, and should be reviewed/confirmed before execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"examples/EXAMPLES.md","start_line":40,"end_line":44}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-d978ecc8fb6449298d86db0725ea4be8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"examples/bulk-delete.json","start_line":21,"end_line":21},"finding":null,"explanation":"The note explicitly advises looping bulk-delete calls until no matching posts remain, which can enable large-scale destructive actions from a broad or mistaken filter. Even though the file says to confirm with the user before sending and limits each call to 100 IDs, the provided workflow still operationalizes mass deletion with little friction and increases the chance of unintended data loss.","remediation":"Require an explicit second confirmation before any repeated or filter-driven bulk deletion, especially when deleting more than one batch. Narrow the example to a single batch, add warnings about previewing matched IDs before deletion, and recommend safeguards such as dry-run listing, maximum deletion thresholds, and human approval for multi-batch delete loops.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"examples/bulk-delete.json","start_line":21,"end_line":21}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-f4da18bc34984334beb355d0532b742b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"examples/youtube-video-captions.json","start_line":4,"end_line":20},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file includes natural-language content stating captions are available in English and also hard-codes the YouTube language to \"en\". Because no user opt-in, language selection, or justification for restricting locale is present, this appears to violate the language/locale policy requirement.","remediation":"Allow the language/caption locale to be selected by the user or document a clear, justified reason that this skill is English-only. If the skill is intended for multiple audiences, make `youtubeLanguage` configurable and update the content text accordingly.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"examples/youtube-video-captions.json","start_line":4,"end_line":20}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-9c82516b4d91493797633b73f6d81c1a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/api-reference.md","start_line":393,"end_line":410},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown documents a bulk deletion endpoint and even provides instructions for deleting everything matching a filter, but it does not include any explicit warning about irreversible removal of posts, schedules, analytics, or associated media. Because this is a destructive operation described in user-facing documentation, the file should clearly warn users before they automate or invoke mass deletion.","remediation":"Add a visible warning near the bulk-delete section stating that the operation removes posts, schedules, and analytics from PostFast and may also remove media once unreferenced. Recommend explicit user confirmation and careful filtering before running the documented delete-all loop.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-reference.md","start_line":393,"end_line":410}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-b3fd8eed38ca4636b86054d4e28f8e5e","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.5,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":32,"end_line":null},"finding":"https://api.postfa.st/","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"## Step 1: Get Signed Upload URLs\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://api.postfa.st/file/get-signed-upload-urls \\\n  -H \"pf-api-key: $POSTFAST_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"aa8d70e9b18461bfce78a3e3a63df6d072055fbb1c3be7fb27250147faa6f9fa","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":32,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-b3fd8eed38ca4636b86054d4e28f8e5e","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.5,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":53,"end_line":null},"finding":"https://api.postfa.st/","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_